# Agent guide

This repository is {{ if .DisplayName }}{{ .DisplayName }}{{ else }}{{ .Container }}{{ end }}, the `{{ .Container }}` operator of {{ .SoftwareSystem }}: a
Kubernetes operator in Go, scaffolded by C4 Factory with kubebuilder and the
`{{ .Standard }}` Standard. Build it to the rules below. What the operator is for,
and what it must never do, is in the issue you were given and the system's
needs: follow those.

## The one rule

`make check` must pass before every commit. It checks that `go.mod` is tidy and
that the generated files are what `make manifests generate` writes, that the
code is formatted (gofmt, goimports), then runs `go vet`, golangci-lint with
`.golangci.yml` and `go test -race` with envtest (a real API server and etcd,
no cluster). CI runs the same command, and nothing reaches `main` without it
passing and a review. Never commit red.

